: session.tool.input.delta, carrying a tool call's arguments as they arrive.
: 
: Everything but the three delta frames is a live capture from OpenCode
: 2.0.1 -- a `shell` call in /tmp/muqun-gw-c1 on a free model. The deltas
: are written to the schema the 2.0.1 binary declares, because neither free
: model streams tool arguments; both jump from input.started to input.ended.
: The binary declares the three events as:
: 
:   let r = {...e, assistantMessageID: ot, id: t}
:   Started = ({type:"session.tool.input.started", schema:{...r, name: t}})
:   Delta   = ({type:"session.tool.input.delta",   schema:{...r, delta: t}})
:   Ended   = ({type:"session.tool.input.ended",   schema:{...r, text: t}})
: 
: and both of its own consumers concatenate the chunks and then replace the
: result with `text` when the call ends:
: 
:   o.raw = (o.raw ?? "") + t.data.delta
:   input: t.type === "session.tool.input.ended"
:            ? t.data.text : s.part.state.input + t.data.delta

